or $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{180}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{36}^{∘}+n\\cdot {144}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={108}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={252}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions are $x={108}^{∘},{252}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ is $108+252=360.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-121557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5332dc810971e60b916abd9b0e55d9218eba7203ce03d9ad3b3e445125c686e9"} {"question" "q-121557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-121557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "328"] ["math" "330"] ["math" "346"] ["math" "360"] ["math" "374"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-121557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "360"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3},$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+{30}^{∘} & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={60}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={30}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={210}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={210}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5332dc810971e60b916abd9b0e55d9218eba7203ce03d9ad3b3e445125c686e9"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328331" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "210"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-274700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)=-1,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,\\,{x}_{2}=$ \n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\,{x}_{3}=$ \n{{field-3}}$,\\,\\,{x}_{4}=$ \n{{field-4}}$,\\,\\,{x}_{5}=$ \n{{field-5}}$,\\,\\,{x}_{6}=$ \n{{field-6}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-274700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n-1)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=4$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$\n\n- Setting $n=5$ gives $x=\\frac{19\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=6$ gives $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{7\\pi }{12},\\,\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{11\\pi }{12},\\,\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\\,{x}_{5}=\\frac{19\\pi }{12},\\,\\,{x}_{6}=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-274700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5332dc810971e60b916abd9b0e55d9218eba7203ce03d9ad3b3e445125c686e9"} {"question" "q-274700" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question