pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(3n+2)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=4$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=5$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=6$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=7$ gives $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}, \\\\ {x}_{5} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{6}=\\frac{17\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{7}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{8}=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5332dc810971e60b916abd9b0e55d9218eba7203ce03d9ad3b3e445125c686e9"} {"question" "q-328359" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328359" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6