home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328359" "field" "field-8" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328359" "field" "field-8" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{23\\pi}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})+4=0,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})+4 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={0}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={90}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={270}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={0}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={90}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={270}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5332dc810971e60b916abd9b0e55d9218eba7203ce03d9ad3b3e445125c686e9"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979276/state.json" "file_sha256" "62ea9c49f08bd409be7ffd561be4195f6d7ba142cfc13259e19cc3e1543ee9a3"} {"question" "q-328351" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r